u can do a bunch of things like customize your crab and pick from a decent amount of guns and you can make your crab have what ever type of load out you want to do", "timestamp_created": 1699964395, "timestamp_updated": 1699964395, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.511794030666351318", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150108738", "author": {"steamid": "76561198008749599", "personaname": "Rhizzy", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/donrade/", "num_games_owned": 1098, "num_reviews": 184, "playtime_forever": 1351, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1173, "last_played": 1710284032, "avatar": "4eaf6f8f0c5f059037c02c77557ca4abcfb6bd0c"}, "language": "english", "review": "This is not just a meme game. It’s a legit roguelike arena shooter that is actually pretty damn fun. The combat is super fast paced. The shooting is smooth and responsive. The visual effects, with all the colorful explosions, are cool. Even the soundtrack is great. \n\nThe perk combinations are interesting but it kinda feels like there is only a handful of builds, or that eventually all builds revolve around some type of crazy AoE mixture. Additionally, after a couple of loops you get super overpowered so going into infinity feels kinda pointless. Though there is a nightmare difficulty and a bunch of modifiers to make things harder. I think the game needs a bunch of secrets, hidden levels, portals, things to discover... kinda like Risk of Rain 2 does it. Maybe even different crab characters that will offer different playstyles (again like RoR2).\n\nThe game is very satisfying to play but after the initial discovery period, trying out all the guns, or unlocking all the achievements, there is not much reason to keep coming back to it. There is about 10-20h of content currently, but a lot more promised and 2+ years of development, so eventually there should be more things to discover. Though even in its current state, the game is worth checking out!", "timestamp_created": 1699959844, "timestamp_updated": 1699959844, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.511794030666351318", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150104746", "author": {"steamid": "76561198109222504", "personaname": "LinxNight", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198109222504/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 3193, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2110, "last_played": 1774321219, "avatar": "ece6d5b4be21c45a5d5dc46a70fd8b3fb2589f51"}, "language": "english", "review": "Fun gaming loop, decent graphics, runs well on my low end laptop. One of my favorite rogue-likes", "timestamp_created": 1699951545, "timestamp_updated": 1699951545, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150101713", "author": {"steamid": "76561198089981228", "personaname": "LarryIRL", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/LarryIRL_/", "num_games_owned": 594, "num_reviews": 34, "playtime_forever": 6808, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5377, "last_played": 1764758757, "avatar": "0a32a144fd69b86a62f68680ed10f85408a9471e"}, "language": "english", "review": "is good", "timestamp_created": 1699944293, "ti